@startuml bau-matching-pipeline
title Use: match an experienced candidate to many jobs (v2 BAU)

skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor "Candidate /\nRecruiter" as user
participant "/api/match" as api
participant "KO Filter" as ko
database "jobs · requirements\n· entry_profiles" as jobs
participant "Multi-factor Scorer" as scorer
participant "Taxonomy graph" as taxo
participant "Reasoning Generator" as reason
participant "reasoning-cache" as rcache
participant "Claude CLI" as claude
database "matches · reasoning" as mstore

user -> api : run matching for candidateId
api -> jobs : load active jobs

== Layer A: hard filters (KO criteria, cheap DB-side) ==
api -> ko : candidate profile + job set
ko -> ko : drop on work-mode preference (remote/hybrid/onsite)
ko -> ko : drop on seniority floor (junior !-> senior-only)
ko -> ko : drop on min education / required languages
ko -> ko : early-career: gate on role entry-eligibility
ko --> api : surviving job shortlist (e.g. 5k -> ~200)

== Layer B: multi-factor scoring (per surviving job) ==
loop each shortlisted job
  api -> scorer : score(candidate, job)
  scorer -> taxo : skills match w/ hierarchy + alias resolution
  scorer -> scorer : career fit (role family + seniority proximity)
  scorer -> scorer : personal fit (language coverage + keyword overlap)
  scorer -> scorer : weighted total by archetype
end
scorer --> api : scored + ranked jobs

== Layer C: LLM reasoning (top-N only, cached) ==
loop top-N ranked
  api -> rcache : lookup(candidateId x jobId, PROMPT_VERSION)
  alt cached
    rcache --> api : reasoning
  else
    api -> reason : generate verdict / strengths / gaps / probes
    reason -> claude : structured call
    claude --> reason : reasoning JSON (else deterministic fallback)
    reason -> rcache : store
    reason --> api : reasoning
  end
end

api -> mstore : persist matches + reasoning
api --> user : ranked list with scores + reasons

note over ko, reason
  Three layers, increasing cost:
  cheap KO filter narrows the corpus,
  deterministic scoring ranks survivors,
  expensive LLM reasoning runs only on the top-N.
  Student mode (diagrams 07-10) swaps the
  filter gates and scoring weights but reuses
  this exact 3-layer skeleton.
end note
@enduml
